WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.980
This is the Singularity Daily, for Friday, November 13.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.490
Here's what happened in superintelligence in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.720
Jensen Huang, the man who built Nvidia,

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:21.080
has resigned as its boss. But the show goes on.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.430
Nvidia's new chair says its plans should carry on "without interruption."

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.970
Meanwhile, Google launched Gemini 4 Hydrogen,

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.150
its new everyday model, replacing Flash across its products.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:45.070
Google says it's 2.5x faster, with over 5x fewer made-up claims.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:52.420
OpenAI reportedly raised $15 billion, at a $1.25 trillion valuation.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.830
And demand for Anthropic's shares is reportedly about six times what's on offer.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.260
Now, the money.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:07.550
SpaceX plans to spend $74 billion on AI data centers in Texas and Arizona.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.560
Google alone pays SpaceX $920 million a month for computing power.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.020
Agile Robots, from Germany,

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:21.520
raised half a billion dollars. It's now worth $8.5 billion.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.050
And AMD is investing in quantum startup PsiQuantum.

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:29.600
Together they're simulating cancer drug molecules.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.360
Now,

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:37.380
the forecasters behind "AI 2027" expect a superhuman AI researcher next year.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.080
By their estimate, AI is already speeding up AI research by 1.7 times.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.480
The catch? Nonprofits are suing OpenAI, Google,

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.590
Anthropic and others to halt frontier AI.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.800
And brain implant maker Synchron paused its trials over a cable problem.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.240
Robots, though, are getting jobs.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.910
Logistics giant GXO plans up to 1,000 humanoids over four years.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.790
J.P. Morgan says American humanoid production could hit 400,000 by 2030.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:21.480
And Google and Samsung's Gemini smart glasses are up for preorder, from $395.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.700
Leaders come and go, even legends.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.740
What they build keeps going. The show goes on.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.030
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.000
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.030
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
